{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1481216-how-to-gain-quintessence-without-a-node","id":1481216,"title":"How to gain Quintessence without a Node?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-05-16T01:33:04-07:00","id":1481216,"title":"How to gain Quintessence without a Node?","content":"I'm running a ?Mage campaign and my group of players doesn't have a Node they can access, some of them have Prime but their highest rating is 3 dots, and they've decided that they want a bunch of Quintessence to prepare for a trip into the underworld. <br /> <br /> How can a Mage gain/regain Quintessence without a Node or high levels of Prime?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-16T02:13:16-07:00","id":1481217,"title":"","content":"And Prime 1-3?<br /> <br /> 1) Invest in Backgrounds like Legend (which generates Quintessence when you embody said Legend), and Wonder (periapts are ones specifically for this purpose, but hard going to be hard to recharge once they're out).<br /> <br /> 2) Tass is the simplest source mechanically, but that means getting it somehow. (and not all Tass is going to be convenient for long journeys).<br /> <br /> 3) Prime 3 is enough to gain Quintessence from ritual sacrifice, either the mage doing damage to themselves for it, or things like the ritual sacrifice of animals.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-16T03:43:11-07:00","id":1481221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1481216-how-to-gain-quintessence-without-a-node#post1481216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm running a ?Mage campaign and my group of players doesn't have a Node they can access, some of them have Prime but their highest rating is 3 dots, and they've decided that they want a bunch of Quintessence to prepare for a trip into the underworld.<br /> <br /> How can a Mage gain/regain Quintessence without a Node or high levels of Prime?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It used to only take Avatar background, prime 3 and Patience.<br /> <br /> The avatar background used to give you it's dot rating in quintessence every day and since Prime 3 allows you to store quintessence in objects, With both and a month of down time you could could essentially Ludicrous amount of quintessence in any objects you were going to take with you anyway.<br /> <br /> Currently the only way to do something similar is the &quot;Nephilim/Laham&quot; merit(7 point merit, M20 book of secrets). Basically it makes your mage half spirit/demon/angel/whatever fits your backstory. The trait gives you the equivalent of 7 quintessence that refresh every day, but does give you the ability to channel, so without Prime or an Avatar rating you're limited to spending 1 quintessence every round. It also comes with an mandatory 3 point in physical flaws that give you no freebies(but they also don't count for your flaw limits).<br /> <br /> Since this is post character creation, a Nephilim Merit NPC + Prime 3 is your best bet for storing large scale quintessence supplies currently unless you want your players killing things on-mass to supply prime 3 rituals(or trying to mug super-naturals).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6383,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","user":"Prometheas","date":". 05-16-2022, 06:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-16T05:34:02-07:00","id":1481231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1481216-how-to-gain-quintessence-without-a-node?p=1481221#post1481221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Since this is post character creation, a Nephilim Merit NPC + Prime 3 is your best bet for storing large scale quintessence supplies currently unless you want your players killing things on-mass to supply prime 3 rituals(or trying to mug super-naturals).</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Magical muggers attack local stiffs downtown, like the hobo furries were not problem enough, what is the prince doing to assure the undead populace's security?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Prince is not a mayor. Also dead, almost as much as Prince's musical career. Plus, you're talking to a graffitti-covered trash bin, Ozzie you ugly sob - stop leeching from stoners, you're sounding like someone on Malk dementia.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 05-30-2022, 02:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-16T05:44:49-07:00","id":1481232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1481216-how-to-gain-quintessence-without-a-node?p=1481231#post1481231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Magical muggers attack local stiffs downtown, like the hobo furries were not problem enough, what is the prince doing to assure the undead populace's security?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Prince is not a mayor. Also dead, almost as much as Prince's musical career. Plus, you're talking to a graffitti-covered trash bin Ozzie you ugly sob - stop leeching from stoners, you're sounding like someone on Malk dementia.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Why is it that the harder WoD writers try to lean on the setting's horror and survival elements, the more they inevitably create opportunities for unintentional comedy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-16T08:43:44-07:00","id":1481240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1481216-how-to-gain-quintessence-without-a-node?p=1481232#post1481232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why is it that the harder WoD writers try to lean on the setting's horror and survival elements, the more they inevitably create opportunities for unintentional comedy?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Because comedy is a natural response and coping/defense mechanism of the human mind against the horrors of the world in the search for meaning to our continued survival. Anyway, the Name of the Rose is your friend and explains. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-16T09:13:40-07:00","id":1481242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1481216-how-to-gain-quintessence-without-a-node?p=1481217#post1481217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And Prime 1-3?<br /> 2) Tass is the simplest source mechanically, but that means getting it somehow. (and not all Tass is going to be convenient for long journeys).</div> </div> </div> </div>On that end: If there are friendly (or neutral) mages that <i>do </i>have a Node arround, Tass it's a common payment for favors. <br /> <br /> If they have something to bargain for it, could be a good way to get the magical bateries. If the other mages want something from the Underworld, the trip by itself could be a bargaining chip.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-24T09:42:35-07:00","id":1481848,"title":"","content":"With Prime 3 (maybe 2) you can pull quintessence from all kinds of sources. With Prime 1, you can find those sources. The characters can drive around (or fly if they have Forces 2) looking for any source of free quintessence. These are often weak nodes (temporary or permanent), and at least some are likely to be undiscovered/unguarded. They can also be things like objects of worship or adoration... Is the Mona Lisa on display? Travel to the museum and get the free quintessence generated by all the people who visit and adore it. If the characters have Correspondence/Data 2 there is no need to even travel there in the flesh.<br /> <br /> Quintessence is everywhere, it's just a matter of finding unguarded sources of free quintessence (or guarded sources if they're willing to take it by force).<br /> <br /> A search for quintessence could make for a fun game session in and of itself.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26904-breggie","name":"breggie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26904_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-24T13:16:11-07:00","id":1481857,"title":"","content":"Taking advantage of a Wellspring (when an event generates enough emotional energy in a bunch of people that it can be harvested as quintessence) requires Prime 4.<br /> <br /> Quintessence is, in fact, everywhere. But the more subtle its expression the higher level Prime you need to effectively get at it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-25T09:16:26-07:00","id":1481928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1481216-how-to-gain-quintessence-without-a-node?p=1481857#post1481857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Taking advantage of a Wellspring (when an event generates enough emotional energy in a bunch of people that it can be harvested as quintessence) requires Prime 4.<br /> <br /> Quintessence is, in fact, everywhere. But the more subtle its expression the higher level Prime you need to effectively get at it.</div> </div> </div> </div>With Prime 4, going through the effort to seek out Wellsprings is the hard way.<br /> <br /> If you're willing to do something vulgar or you have a sanctum to make it coincidental, you can just pick up rocks and &quot;unmake&quot; them, converting them directly to quintessence and gobbling it up.<br /> <br /> As for lower levels of Prime, you might be able to easily find nodes depending on the storyteller, I guess. My ST has always made weak nodes common enough that they can be found with some effort, and there is a good chance weak ones are unguarded or undiscovered, so gathering small to moderate amounts of quintessence has never been much of an issue for a character with at least Prime 1.<br /> <br /> That said, I acknowledge that this may not be RAW, but the OP says they are the ST and so ultimately the answer could be up to them if they want to houserule something. Quintessence is vital to any significant undertaking for a Mage, and so any player who did not anticipate that at character creation and buy a Node is completely hamstrung until they get really high Prime magick... I find that rules design decision to be... weird. And unfortunate.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26904,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26904-breggie","user":"breggie","date":". 05-25-2022, 12:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26904-breggie","name":"breggie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26904_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-25T12:58:12-07:00","id":1481947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>breggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1481216-how-to-gain-quintessence-without-a-node?p=1481928#post1481928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With Prime 4, going through the effort to seek out Wellsprings is the hard way.</div> </div> </div> </div>... that's what trying to get quintessence out of art tourists is. You can't get quintessence from the Mona Lisa below Prime 4 unless you plan on destroying it. Prime 4 is when you get to soak up the ambient quintessence of lots of people having a shared emotional experience<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you're willing to do something vulgar or you have a sanctum to make it coincidental, you can just pick up rocks and &quot;unmake&quot; them, converting them directly to quintessence and gobbling it up. </div> </div> </div>How much quintessence do you think any old random rock is worth?<br /> <br /> One of the things Prime and Primal Utility agree on is that how much quintessence something can generate is based on worth. They disagree in how worth is determined. To normal mystic Prime, worth is sympathetic value: the more magically special something is, the more quintessence it can hold. A large rock you found in the dirt generates less quintessence upon unmaking than the Blarney Stone, because if you unmake the Blarney Stone you're not just destroying some rock, you're destroying all the sympathetic connections and resonance that one specific rock has. The Blarney Stone doesn't have to be tass, or a Wonder, or whatever. It's worth more because of all the worth humans have poured into it.<br /> <br /> From a game-design perspective the point here is simple: Nodes (or similar phenomena) and tass would be worthless if mages could burn their junk mail in their sanctums for significant quantities of quintessence. Since burning junk mail with Prime to unmake it is not particularly difficult, the only way to make sure the normal methods of obtaining quintessence are desirable is to make how much quintessence junk mail has in it very small. If it takes 100 lbs of junk mail to get 1 quintessence, it's not worthless to have that ability, but it's not exactly going to be something most mages are going to find practical. The same applies to rocks, tree branches, or whatever.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for lower levels of Prime, you might be able to easily find nodes depending on the storyteller, I guess. </div> </div> </div>Prime 1, alone, is limited to your direct sensory range, but otherwise can find any Node/etc. that happens to be around and isn't being hidden by stronger magics. Though that's a very good way to get into a lot of trouble.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My ST has always made weak nodes common enough that they can be found with some effort, and there is a good chance weak ones are unguarded or undiscovered, so gathering small to moderate amounts of quintessence has never been much of an issue for a character with at least Prime 1. </div> </div> </div>That is, of course, your ST's prerogative, but not really that in-keeping with the books as presented. Mages would not risk major conflicts with each other, or other supernaturals, over Nodes if there's enough of them that a bunch of low level ones are around in any area completely unclaimed and unguarded.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-26T06:45:44-07:00","id":1481992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1481216-how-to-gain-quintessence-without-a-node?p=1481947#post1481947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> All the stuff...<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>All good points, and ultimately I agree. I guess it's just that I don't really care for the game design of &quot;if you didn't realize you needed a node at CC then you are just SOL. Make a new character or wait until you can buy Prime 4&quot;.<br /> <br /> Then again, I can't really think of much that you absolutely need quintessence for except for making Wonders, and that likewise requires Prime 4. A Prime 2/3 mage is a bit SOL without quintessence if they want to make trinkets and charms/gadgets I guess. You need quintessence to heal aggravated damage with Life, but I think Entropy 4 can heal any damage without expending quintessence, so at least there's a workaround for some mages.<br /> <br /> Then again, again, if a character needs quintessence it can become a story arc to find and secure a node. It will likely require violence, but ultimately satisfying a character's needs is a major source of material for that character's story, including acquiring backgrounds like Node.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26904-breggie","name":"breggie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26904_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-26T07:41:45-07:00","id":1481995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1481216-how-to-gain-quintessence-without-a-node?p=1481947#post1481947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How much quintessence do you think any old random rock is worth?<br /> <br /> One of the things Prime and Primal Utility agree on is that how much quintessence something can generate is based on worth. They disagree in how worth is determined. To normal mystic Prime, worth is sympathetic value: the more magically special something is, the more quintessence it can hold. A large rock you found in the dirt generates less quintessence upon unmaking than the Blarney Stone, because if you unmake the Blarney Stone you're not just destroying some rock, you're destroying all the sympathetic connections and resonance that one specific rock has. The Blarney Stone doesn't have to be tass, or a Wonder, or whatever. It's worth more because of all the worth humans have poured into it.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's inherent issues with trying to assign quintessence value based on &quot;worth&quot; though. Worth is subjective, Especially metaphysical worth because metaphysic themselves are subjective. What looks to one mage like a useless rock is a rare form of sacred granite to another and Scientist might get a Buttload of quintessence from &quot;useless rock&quot; because they use a physics-based paradigm that says all matter has exponentially more energy the more mass it has.<br /> <br /> Not sure there's actually a solution to that problem though. Narratively it comes down to what the ST needs for the story to work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1481216-how-to-gain-quintessence-without-a-node?p=1481947#post1481947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From a game-design perspective the point here is simple: Nodes (or similar phenomena) and tass would be worthless if mages could burn their junk mail in their sanctums for significant quantities of quintessence. Since burning junk mail with Prime to unmake it is not particularly difficult, the only way to make sure the normal methods of obtaining quintessence are desirable is to make how much quintessence junk mail has in it very small. If it takes 100 lbs of junk mail to get 1 quintessence, it's not worthless to have that ability, but it's not exactly going to be something most mages are going to find practical. The same applies to rocks, tree branches, or whatever.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I don't see a problem with mages having ways to get lots of quintessence using prime unmaking. Nodes are still required to make chantries and power certain wonders, large amounts of loose quintessence will get burned through too quickly to be able to fill that gap.<br /> <br /> Besides, if you look at prime too closely you'll notice quintessence rarity is as balance as a D&amp;D gold economy, there are just too many ways to break it and undermine that assumption that gold/quint is rare. Quintessence being hard to get is entirely a setting handwave.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-26T08:17:21-07:00","id":1481998,"title":"","content":"Hunt some vampires and harvest their blood for tass. Doesn't have the best resonance but you are doing the world a service and getting tass for it!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5617-vendrin","name":"Vendrin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-26T08:57:15-07:00","id":1482000,"title":"","content":"Wait, cant you trade your own HP for Quint anymore with Prime 1?<br /> <br /> It use to be that you could keep burning your 1st health level to trade for Quint in a daily basis with only Prime 1","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-26T10:55:15-07:00","id":1482009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1481216-how-to-gain-quintessence-without-a-node?p=1482000#post1482000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, cant you trade your own HP for Quint anymore with Prime 1?<br /> <br /> It use to be that you could keep burning your 1st health level to trade for Quint in a daily basis with only Prime 1</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you can still do that. Ouch!, but feasible.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Now reading it on HDYDT, it's unclear to me if you can *keep* the Quintessence on your wheel, or it has to be used immediately (as the example there on Heart's Blood only covers powering an effect). I would allow it to be keept, tho.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 05-26-2022, 02:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-26T11:10:01-07:00","id":1482012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>breggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1481216-how-to-gain-quintessence-without-a-node?p=1481992#post1481992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess it's just that I don't really care for the game design of &quot;if you didn't realize you needed a node at CC then you are just SOL. Make a new character or wait until you can buy Prime 4&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is... you're not SoL if you don't start with a Node. It just means you lack one specific resource under your direct control. Your Mentor has one, but gets to veto you using it, let alone your whole Cabal using it. Etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Then again, I can't really think of much that you absolutely need quintessence for except for making Wonders, and that likewise requires Prime 4. </div> </div> </div>That is, ultimately, one of the reasons that the game goes with a relative scarcity of Nodes/etc. You really don't need them outside of very specific circumstances; those specifics are very important to mage society as a whole, but not that important to daily life as an individual mage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1481216-how-to-gain-quintessence-without-a-node?p=1481995#post1481995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's inherent issues with trying to assign quintessence value based on &quot;worth&quot; though. Worth is subjective, Especially metaphysical worth because metaphysic themselves are subjective.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh. One one hand yes, but on the other if you're playing Ascension you've already mastered this skill because it applies to so much of the game as it is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Besides, if you look at prime too closely you'll notice quintessence rarity is as balance as a D&amp;D gold economy, there are just too many ways to break it and undermine that assumption that gold/quint is rare. Quintessence being hard to get is entirely a setting handwave. </div> </div> </div>I think there's a certain white-room analysis here that don't quite work. What high level Prime can do regarding increasing access to quintessence isn't 1-3 success simple feats of magic. They're innately high difficulty, and easily fall into lots and lots of successes needed to make work. The expense and difficulty of mastering Spheres also means there aren't that many Prime 4+ mages running around at any given moment in the setting to &quot;break the economy.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1481216-how-to-gain-quintessence-without-a-node?p=1482000#post1482000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, cant you trade your own HP for Quint anymore with Prime 1?<br /> <br /> It use to be that you could keep burning your 1st health level to trade for Quint in a daily basis with only Prime 1</div> </div> </div> </div>It's still there, but a bit more constrained:<br /> <br /> 1) It's 1 quintessence/HL, so it's only 1/day max if you want to rely on natural healing.<br /> <br /> 2) It costs 1 quintessence to heal if you need to heal it early, so it nets to zero under stress.<br /> <br /> 3) Healing agg requires significant rest. You're not supposed to do that, and then spend a day doing hard ritual magic, or getting into combat, and expect to regain that health. <br /> <br /> Basically, it's supposed to be much more of a desperation tactic rather than a normal daily routine thing for most mages, because most mages don't want to spend 24 hrs doing bedrest for 1 quintessence.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-29T19:10:39-07:00","id":1482319,"title":"","content":"The best way in the end is to seek Tass, it is the most versatile way to find free Quintessence for both characters and ST. Chantries and individual mages may have small (or not so small) hoards of Tass, sometimes you can find still usable Tass a certain distance from the source Node for reasons, and anyone keeping a Node also has Tass no matter how they call it, or even notice it.<br /> <br /> What you do once you find a source of Tass is up to you. You can take the place by force, sure, but you can also focus on stealing just the Tass, or trading it for something or some service. That basically means that a character looking for Tass will find it with relative ease if they're not picky and are ready to deal with whatever holds this Tass, and the ST may include some Tass behind any interesting task whatsoever. Add some complications on how to preserve some of it during the trip and you're ready to go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-01T04:27:50-07:00","id":1482589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1481216-how-to-gain-quintessence-without-a-node?p=1482012#post1482012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The thing is... you're not SoL if you don't start with a Node. It just means you lack one specific resource under your direct control. Your Mentor has one, but gets to veto you using it, let alone your whole Cabal using it. Etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could also have a Periapt (sorry, I dont even know if that's the proper word in english; english is not my mother tongue and my Mage book is a translated version, so I dont even know the original word. If it's not, I mean the Quint battery artifact)<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think there's a certain white-room analysis here that don't quite work. What high level Prime can do regarding increasing access to quintessence isn't 1-3 success simple feats of magic. They're innately high difficulty, and easily fall into lots and lots of successes needed to make work. The expense and difficulty of mastering Spheres also means there aren't that many Prime 4+ mages running around at any given moment in the setting to &amp;quot;break the economy.&amp;quot; </div> </div> </div>Yeah, well, at least in a Chantry isnt a vulgar effect.<br /> <br /> That reminds me of a theoretical effect I thought, let me hear your opinion on it: could it be possible to create a PERMANENT Prime 4 effect that generates a sort of &quot;disintegrator&quot; area, upon which anything throw inside would be... well, disintegrated lol, into its Quintessential components?<br /> <br /> That could become a powerful addition / replacement for Nodes. &quot;Just throw it into the recicler&quot; with a whole different meaning.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's still there, but a bit more constrained:<br /> <br /> 1) It's 1 quintessence/HL, so it's only 1/day max if you want to rely on natural healing.<br /> <br /> 2) It costs 1 quintessence to heal if you need to heal it early, so it nets to zero under stress.<br /> <br /> 3) Healing agg requires significant rest. You're not supposed to do that, and then spend a day doing hard ritual magic, or getting into combat, and expect to regain that health. <br /> <br /> Basically, it's supposed to be much more of a desperation tactic rather than a normal daily routine thing for most mages, because most mages don't want to spend 24 hrs doing bedrest for 1 quintessence. </div> </div> </div>Yes, indeed it can only be done on a one-by-one daily tactic, and to grab one tiny point. Still, it could serve those less fortunate that want some Quint so desperately. A few weeks in bad with high protein food and just reading your thaumatological books or your engineer manuals without practicing them much, just theory, is still doable. A whole month delving in theorical magic as opposed to practical in bad is enough to garner 30 Quint! Which is a very considerable amount.<br /> <br /> An inconvenience, sure, but possible.<br /> <br /> And an entire Cabal could gather enough for building their own Periapt (which of course would require Prime 4)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-01T05:30:07-07:00","id":1482592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1481216-how-to-gain-quintessence-without-a-node?p=1482589#post1482589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You could also have a Periapt (sorry, I dont even know if that's the proper word in english; english is not my mother tongue and my Mage book is a translated version, so I dont even know the original word. If it's not, I mean the Quint battery artifact)<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Periapt is correct. Matrix for a Technocrat.<br /> <br /> Do Peripats refill on their own even without a node? My cyborg character has a 1-point Matrix implanted in his chest... does this mean he has a self-refilling battery of 5 quintessence? I thought it was just extra &quot;storage&quot;...<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26904-breggie","name":"breggie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26904_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-01T07:01:04-07:00","id":1482600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1481216-how-to-gain-quintessence-without-a-node?p=1482589#post1482589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That reminds me of a theoretical effect I thought, let me hear your opinion on it: could it be possible to create a PERMANENT Prime 4 effect that generates a sort of &quot;disintegrator&quot; area, upon which anything throw inside would be... well, disintegrated lol, into its Quintessential components?<br /> <br /> That could become a powerful addition / replacement for Nodes. &quot;Just throw it into the recicler&quot; with a whole different meaning.</div> </div> </div> </div>The most practical way would be to make a Talisman with two Prime effects triggered when something is put in it: one to unmake and one to channel quintessence, that then recharges a periapt (not a proper noun and an obscure enough word that there's no reason to capitalize it for system notation to differentiate between like Wonder and wonder). Though you'd lose any quintessence in excess of the available storage space. If you added some Matter (or Life but that's probably not the best idea) you could have it produce tass instead.<br /> <br /> Doing it as an ongoing magical effect runs into a lot of complications.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> An inconvenience, sure, but possible. </div> </div> </div>Being under bed rest conditions for a month is more than just a mild inconvenience. It's mentally traumatic. Most doctors would put you on a mild anti-depressant to proactively avoid cabin fever if they were expecting a patient to be in that state for that long.<br /> <br /> Yes, possible, but an ordeal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>breggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1481216-how-to-gain-quintessence-without-a-node?p=1482592#post1482592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Peripats refill on their own even without a node?</div> </div> </div> </div>They don't refill on their own, but you can refill them without a Node if you have enough Prime and access to some other source of quintessence.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-01T08:00:36-07:00","id":1482605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1481216-how-to-gain-quintessence-without-a-node?p=1482600#post1482600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They don't refill on their own, but you can refill them without a Node if you have enough Prime and access to some other source of quintessence.</div> </div> </div> </div>On that note, can Prime 3 break down tass and absorb it into a periapt or into personal quintessence (based on Avatar rating or exceeding it by using Prime 1)?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26904-breggie","name":"breggie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26904_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-01T08:54:18-07:00","id":1482607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>breggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1481216-how-to-gain-quintessence-without-a-node?p=1482605#post1482605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On that note, can Prime 3 break down tass and absorb it into a periapt or into personal quintessence (based on Avatar rating or exceeding it by using Prime 1)?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I dont remember what I said about it in M20, but my 3th edition I remember it said that it had to be used... Althought, again, that's one of the many things I never agreed with... If the Quintessence is freed, it is freed, so it should be storageable...<br /> <br /> By then again, I also never liked allowing Prime 1 to &quot;de-quintesynthesize&quot; yourself... And since we are into that, neither do I like Life 2 to heal self.<br /> <br /> You see, you had that little table about &quot;number of successes&quot; that stated that &quot;you require no additional successes to affect self; one additional success per target&quot;.<br /> <br /> Soooo... You dont see people using Time 2 to speed themselves instead of Time 3 just because... Therefore I dont see why &quot;self&quot; should earn less magik knowledge instead of simply being easier to cast.<br /> <br /> Which is why sucking the Quint from self blood is Prime 4 in my tables, and self heal is still Life 3. But that's me of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-01T09:05:45-07:00","id":1482608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1481216-how-to-gain-quintessence-without-a-node?p=1482600#post1482600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The most practical way would be to make a Talisman with two Prime effects triggered when something is put in it: one to unmake and one to channel quintessence, that then recharges a periapt (not a proper noun and an obscure enough word that there's no reason to capitalize it for system notation to differentiate between like Wonder and wonder). Though you'd lose any quintessence in excess of the available storage space. If you added some Matter (or Life but that's probably not the best idea) you could have it produce tass instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. Interesting. It is possible then. Good to now.<br /> <br /> But I didnt want a Talisman, I really wanted a sort of &quot;static black hole&quot; on the middle of my chantry. In fact, more like a &quot;blue hole&quot;, a globe of blue energy that is used for unmaking stuff to free Quint.<br /> <br /> Aesthetics is everything in the life of a Mage, wouldnt you agree?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Doing it as an ongoing magical effect runs into a lot of complications. </div> </div> </div>Yes, Im sure it would, but that could very well become a &quot;Chantries basic tool kit&quot;. Not a Talisman, things that are jealously hoarded and access controled, but those &quot;unmakers&quot; would instead be for common use.<br /> <br /> Prime 4 Adepts would become respectable &quot;chantry masons&quot; and become enablers for weaker chantries with no nodes and no Adepts.<br /> <br /> Also, consider the cool Aestetics of having one of those cool globes of energy in a dedicated room in every chantry...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Being under bed rest conditions for a month is more than just a mild inconvenience. It's mentally traumatic. Most doctors would put you on a mild anti-depressant to proactively avoid cabin fever if they were expecting a patient to be in that state for that long.<br /> <br /> Yes, possible, but an ordeal. </div> </div> </div>Well... Yes. You're right. Not the most ideal of the circumstances indeed.<br /> <br /> Still, maybe a viable option for desperate circumstances. And the load could be shared too - 5 mages for 5 days wouldnt be so much of an ordeal, and would earn a sizeable 25 quints<br /> <br /> Edit: loved the idea to add Matter to it, using such &quot;device&quot; to create Tass hadnt even cross my mind before... Now I can make my &quot;purificator&quot; to absorb trash and slowly drip purified &quot;energized&quot; water... Cool concept there.<br /> <br /> Althought, as others noticed, that should indeed be a minimal amount of Tass created for massive amounts of trash.<br /> <br /> Still, &quot;minimal&quot; is still better than null","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24689,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","user":"Kakost","date":". 06-01-2022, 12:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-01T11:25:34-07:00","id":1482624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1481216-how-to-gain-quintessence-without-a-node?p=1482608#post1482608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Edit: loved the idea to add Matter to it, using such &quot;device&quot; to create Tass had'nt even cross my mind before... Now I can make my &quot;purificator&quot; to absorb trash and slowly drip purified &quot;energized&quot; water... Cool concept there.<br /> <br /> Although, as others noticed, that should indeed be a minimal amount of Tass created for massive amounts of trash.<br /> <br /> Still, &quot;minimal&quot; is still better than null</div> </div> </div> </div>It is also useful to purify things that are not... palatable, to a mage. You could throw nasty tass (Vitae? Garou brains? I dunno) into it and get out a non-offensive, neutral tass that is much more palatable, probably on a 1:1 ratio or close to it. Or it could just provide hyper-electricity to refill technocratic SPECM.<br /> <br /> I don't know about your character, but my Technocrat would have little use for something like Vitae otherwise.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26904-breggie","name":"breggie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26904_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-01T14:03:58-07:00","id":1482653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>breggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1481216-how-to-gain-quintessence-without-a-node?p=1482605#post1482605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On that note, can Prime 3 break down tass and absorb it into a periapt or into personal quintessence (based on Avatar rating or exceeding it by using Prime 1)?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, though the first is technically two effects (not that either is hard enough that the additional successes to combine them is meaningful unless you try to do a lot of tass at once, or it's an extremely potent piece of tass).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-01T15:30:35-07:00","id":1482672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1481216-how-to-gain-quintessence-without-a-node#post1481216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">they've decided that they want a bunch of Quintessence to prepare for a trip into the underworld.</div> </div> </div> </div>I intuit from this that it is a Traditions Chronicle, since Technocrats generally don't do such voyages.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1481216-how-to-gain-quintessence-without-a-node?p=1482319#post1482319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What you do once you find a source of Tass is up to you. You can take the place by force, sure, but you can also focus on stealing just the Tass, or trading it for something or some service. That basically means that a character looking for Tass will find it with relative ease if they're not picky and are ready to deal with whatever holds this Tass, and the ST may include some Tass behind any interesting task whatsoever. Add some complications on how to preserve some of it during the trip and you're ready to go.</div> </div> </div> </div>Trade, pillage or theft... I have some ideas. From the quick read I just did, I think other posters have covered the subject of Trading for Tass better than I could. it's usually not advisable for Traditions to claim Technocracy ode by force, whether to hold or loot. That leaves stealing.<br /> <br /> Consider, if you have the Spheres, enchanting a Quadcopter. If you have both Prime and Correspondence, stick a Wonder-Drone over the Technomancers house, lab or what have you. Intercept the Quintessence coming down.<br /> <br /> Like mine, you're running a low resource chronicle from outset up to the point you are. Forcing players to be resourceful is actually way more fun than starting with all the goodies. At the very least, your Cabal can detect where Nodes are. There is bound to be someone in the Cabal who has a profession-related attribute at 3. Technology - Electrician (with Science, Electrical Engineer). Medicine 3, IIRK, is pretty close to medical doctor.<br /> <br /> Step 1: One character lands a high paying job. After the first pay-check arrives in their checking account, approach the bank to inquire about purchasing a new home with a <i>Transferable</i> mortgage. Use Mind if needed (the Mind Mage hangs around in line of sight). With support from the bank...<br /> <br /> Step 2: Shop for the lowest price property near the Node. Approach the city and, in the same way as with the bank, ask for planning permission for some renovations. Ask for a dual Residential/Commercial Zoning permit sufficient to run a business from this location.<br /> <br /> 2A) A rural area: Renovate, which will involve Vulgar Magic Without Witnesses. Spend as much Quintessence as you need to improve the outcome of the magic-aspect. Raise the value in whatever way suits your Cabal's skill combination. You want be able to host parties, entertain business clients and have a workshop/lab for magic purposes (making bullet resistant armor, cellular sniffing rods, Quint-Syphon quadcopters, etc.). <br /> <br /> 2B) Suburban: Focus on the commercial aspect. If you need a workshop, prioritize soundproofing. <br /> <br /> 2C) Inner city: As an extra-special bonus, there is usually crime affecting property values. So, you will scout any gantsa-neighbors, learn their secrets, but hold off on shutting them down until you have expanded to your satisfaction. Generate business income and use it to officially hire other members of the Cabal so that they have taxable income and improved credit ratings. Rinse and repeat for every member of the Cabal, Acolyte or whoever. <br /> <br /> The owner of the Node you are starting to surround might take notice. On the other hand, they may not be there, having used the accrued Quintessence / Tass to fund similar expeditions to the one mentioned OP (Void Engineers going to Pluto). Either way, you are far enough back that they have to leave the Node if they want to &quot;visit&quot;, forgoing the advantage that their Node provides where competing magic is concerned. What about the element of surprise? - Time 2. <br /> <br /> If you have a Virtual Adept or other spy-type mage, bug everything; police station, city hall, the bank office, etc. The Node owner may pull connections to thwart your expansion. Record all such conversations and retain a lawyer. At this point, you should be in an improved position to negotiate with Node Owner who your Cabal likely outnumbers. <br /> <br /> In the long run, they have two choices. They can sell, in which case you borrow and buy. They can try to buy up property as you are doing, in which case, you can sell, since what you own has no special metaphysical value and has increased significantly in dollar value. <br /> <br /> Returning to the subject of Trade / Pillage / Steal, there is another option - Subdue. Mages who have a Node, are usually well established enough that they would tend to fit the Network Type of Cabal or Technocracy Team (use to be called Symposium). <br /> <br /> From: <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1477147-cabal-types-member-proximity-public-association-role-in-chantry-mage-society\">Cabal Types</a>: member-proximity, public association, role in Chantry/Mage Society</span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1477147-cabal-types-member-proximity-public-association-role-in-chantry-mage-society#post1477147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will just start with two completely different types of Cabals.<br /> <br /> The first kind is the one players usually play. The Mages live together, go most places together and cast beneficial magic on each other.<br /> <br /> The second more closely fits the definition of a Cabal. Members hide their association with each other and carry out a clandestine agenda in the community. They would make use of a Mindlink to coordinate their activities.</div> </div> </div> </div>The longer a cabal survives, the more it would stretch out, meaning members would be more likely encountered <i>alone</i>. Since, you are a relatively new Cabal, it stands to reason, you would stick together and keep an eye out for anyone with a grenade-launcher. You can gang up on a single mage and cast every type of charm, fatigue or short-term fate (Entropy) spell, only one of which can be countered in a single round. Bring them under your influence, one by one. <br /> <br /> I hope this offers a perspective on strategy that you can derive ideas from, suitable to your own chronicle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-02T07:12:23-07:00","id":1482744,"title":"","content":"Ignore this post, it posted to the wrong thread. I have too many tabs open....<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26904-breggie","name":"breggie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26904_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}